From 7e5c0b38ed828a982f7b827867b7c2578e91ed34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 16:13:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 29/31] ASoC: zhihe: port the A210 audio stack to mainline

The A210's audio support (the sound/soc/zhihe platform drivers and the
es8156/es7210/aw87565 codecs) was dropped during the 6.6.x->mainline port
as part of the headless-server scoping. The board does carry the hardware
(simple-audio-card wired to I2S/TDM/PDM + an ES8156 DAC, ES7210 mic-array
ADC and AW87565 speaker amp), so without it the boot-time simple-card hits
"asoc-simple-card: parse error" and stays in deferred probe.

Re-import the vendor drivers and wire them into the build:
  - sound/soc/zhihe/: I2S, TDM, PDM and the dummy/dmaengine PCM glue
    (SND_SOC_ZHIHE_{I2S,TDM,PDM,PCM}).
  - sound/soc/codecs/: ES8156 DAC, ES7210 ADC, AW87565 amplifier.

Fix the 6.6->7.1 API drift surfaced by re-enabling them:
  - platform_driver .remove now returns void; .remove_new is gone
    (zhihe i2s/tdm/pdm/dummy-pcm).
  - <linux/of_gpio.h> was removed; drop the unused include (aw87565, and
    es8156 where the of_gpio users are dead code under an undefined
    HP_DET_FUNTION; the live path uses the legacy gpio.h API).
  - ASoC clock-master DAIFMT constants renamed to provider/consumer:
    CBM_CFM->CBP_CFP, CBS_CFS->CBC_CFC (es8156).

Co-developed-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
